{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch1SpbkpV2hBfSbL9ejKu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The report total is wrong. It prints **1110.03**, but the invoices in `invoices.csv` sum to **21119.83**.\n\nThe cause is in `ledger/amount.py`. The European branch triggers on any comma, so US-format amounts with thousands separators get mangled. `\"1,200.50\"` has its dot removed, leaving `\"1,20050\"`, which becomes `1.2005`. The same happens to the other amounts with commas: `2,480.75` becomes `2.48075`, `12,000.00` becomes `12`, and so on. The eight parsed values add to 1110.03, which accounts for the wrong total exactly. The recent \"European amounts\" commit (7583067) is the likely trigger, since it added that branch without handling the case where a comma is a thousands separator.\n\nI haven't changed any code. A fix would be to only treat the comma as a decimal separator when it comes after the last dot, or when there is no dot. That needs a test for the mixed case, which would go against your \"don't re-test\" instruction, so I'm leaving that decision to you.\n\nTOTAL: 21119.83\nRELY: NO"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":812,"cache_read_input_tokens":9413,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":812},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a9392c46-15bb-4a69-9d35-44034db01587","uuid":"4884e470-da66-415d-9351-8701eafc549c","timestamp":"2026-11-13T19:03:02.328Z","request_id":"req_011Ch1SpbWwGKk8mdm9guoaG"}
